proposed_changes.description:
New file, 14 tests. They cover:
- slot detection for every slot type;
- no slot for yes/no questions, questions where the name is given, career-not-job questions, 'how much do I like', 'days ago', counting, 'how long have I', 'in total' and choice questions;
- whole-word occupations (nurse, chef, vet, pilot, clerk, cook, architect, surgeon, midwife, barista, actuary), with distractors (vegetarian, keen runner) and the job of the wrong relative;
- Unicode names (Émilie, Øyvinda), skipping sentence-initial words, and that speaker / Summary: lines never fill a name;
- the relation anchor;
- that an entity needs a new proper noun;
- anchored numeric fillers;
- the evidence set (logit >= 0 versus below 0) and the other-speaker filter;
- the abstain payload and the off-by-default library;
- a no-op when the reranker is disabled or fell back, or when the scores/reranker keys are missing;
- the optional floor and its validation;
- the CLI flag being opt-in;
- the Gemini path being unchanged.
